<title>HONG KONG: Shun Ho Construction yr net down 8.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Shun Ho Construction yr net down 8.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 6.5	 vs 7.1 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  nil	 vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	2.00 gain vs 0.91 loss</p>
<p>    Net			  33.07     vs 36.28</p>
<p>    Turnover		   11.61     vs 11.01</p>
<p>    Company name	     Shun Ho Construction (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		June 23-27</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Shun Ho Construction, is 53.36 percent owned by Shun Ho Resources Holdings Ltd, which engages in property investment and building construction.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one-for-20 shares.</p>
<p>During the year the group entered into an agreement for the diposal of its development property. As a result of the purchaser failing to complete the sale, the deposit of HK$2 million received by the group was forfeited and recognised as exceptional gain.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings have been adjusted to take into account the bonus issue of shares made during the year.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
